**Functions (tools) loaded from {tools_path}:**
{tools_names}

**How to add your own functions:** Create the file `config/venice_ai/tools.yaml` and define tools as a YAML list. Each tool needs a `name`, `description`, `type`, and `parameters` block. Venice recognises these tool types: `native` (built-in HA actions), `script` (HA scripts), `template` (Jinja2 templates), `web` (HTTP calls), `bash` (shell commands), `sqlite` (database queries), `file` (read/write files), and `composite` (chain multiple tools). Bundled tools from the integration are always available as a baseline and cannot be removed.
